# Copy to push-android.env and fill in. Mounted into the Android push
# backend via docker-compose `env_file`. Never committed (see
# .gitignore). PUSH_BIND, the store path and the non-secret settings
# are set by docker-compose and .env — don't set them here. Full list:
# onym-push/google/src/config.rs.

# The Google service-account key JSON, on ONE line (fold real newlines
# away — JSON whitespace outside strings is insignificant, and the
# private_key's \n are escaped inside the JSON string, so the folded
# value is the same document; same trick as moderation-android's key).
# ONE service account, TWO scopes: it must be granted both Play
# Integrity (playintegrity.googleapis.com) and Firebase Cloud
# Messaging (fcm.googleapis.com) access. There is a
# PUSH_GOOGLE_SA_KEY_PATH alternative upstream, but this stack has
# nowhere to mount a file the GitHub Actions deploy could also
# produce, so the inline form is the one that works both ways.
# Without it the service registers devices and delivers nothing, and
# accepts registrations on the session signature alone.
PUSH_GOOGLE_SA_KEY_JSON=
